<sheets>
<sheet>
<plain>
<text x="231.394" y="76.962" size="5.08" layer="97">WiFi Block</text>
<text x="160.02" y="132.08" size="2.54" layer="97">NOTE: ESP8266 requires a separate supply</text>
<text x="78.74" y="142.24" size="1.778" layer="91">Remember to get power supply for WIFI that doesn't run from TM4C launchpad!!!!!!!!</text>
<text x="78.74" y="-27.94" size="1.778" layer="91">LEFT TM4C LAUNCHPAD (LIKE ON EXCEL PIN CONNECTOR SHEET)</text>
<text x="381" y="-25.4" size="1.778" layer="91">RIGHT TM4C LAUNCHPAD (LIKE EXCEL PIN CONNECTOR SHEET)</text>
<text x="10.16" y="78.74" size="1.778" layer="91">Try to get a wall wart that is at least 9V output</text>
<text x="38.1" y="198.12" size="1.778" layer="91">5V output</text>
<text x="71.12" y="137.16" size="1.778" layer="91">3.3V output</text>
<text x="7.62" y="205.74" size="1.778" layer="91">This linear regulator powers the two launchpads, LCD, Speaker, round potentiometer, and LEDs</text>
<text x="101.6" y="116.84" size="1.778" layer="91">This linear regulator powers the Wifi Chip, 16 button 3.3V input, 
slide potentiometer (for tone change), and LED switch</text>
<text x="93.98" y="-121.92" size="1.778" layer="91">BUTTONS</text>
<text x="91.44" y="-50.8" size="1.778" layer="91">**NOTE: Must connect Launchpad 2 GPIO button inputs 
without use of traces (aka wires with wire nut) because I can't connect two different nets together</text>
<text x="426.72" y="-86.36" size="1.778" layer="91">LEDs and volume pot below</text>
<text x="93.98" y="-124.46" size="1.778" layer="91">and slide POT</text>
<text x="12.7" y="144.78" size="1.778" layer="91">pin 1 is power</text>
<text x="5.08" y="139.7" size="1.778" layer="91">pin 2 is GND</text>
<text x="10.16" y="83.82" size="1.778" layer="91">pin 3 is to see if something is connected 
(not needed in our circuit)</text>
<text x="215.9" y="185.42" size="1.778" layer="91">GND</text>
<text x="215.9" y="182.88" size="1.778" layer="91">+3.3V</text>
<text x="215.9" y="180.34" size="1.778" layer="91">RST</text>
<text x="215.9" y="177.8" size="1.778" layer="91">D/C</text>
<text x="215.9" y="175.26" size="1.778" layer="91">CARD_CS</text>
<text x="215.9" y="172.72" size="1.778" layer="91">TFT_CS</text>
<text x="215.9" y="170.18" size="1.778" layer="91">MOSI</text>
<text x="215.9" y="167.64" size="1.778" layer="91">SCK</text>
<text x="215.9" y="165.1" size="1.778" layer="91">MISO</text>
<text x="215.9" y="162.56" size="1.778" layer="91">LIGHT</text>
<text x="213.36" y="193.04" size="1.778" layer="91">ST7735LCD</text>
<text x="444.5" y="43.18" size="1.778" layer="91">REMEMBER TO DIRECTLY CONNECT PIN HEADER FOR ROUND POT TO SEE PROPER CONNECTIONS</text>
<text x="27.94" y="-182.88" size="1.778" layer="91">Use these pins as internal Pull down resistor </text>
<text x="312.42" y="99.06" size="1.778" layer="91">REMEMBER TO CHANGE NET NAMES FOR OUTB ON 
TLV5618 DAC!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!</text>
<text x="408.94" y="73.66" size="1.778" layer="91">REMEMBER TO CHANGE NET NAMES FOR OUTB ON 
TLV5618 DAC!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!</text>
<text x="309.88" y="2.54" size="1.778" layer="91">REMEMBER TO CHANGE NET NAMES FOR OUTB ON 
TLV5618 DAC!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!</text>
<text x="139.7" y="-182.88" size="1.778" layer="91">Use these pins as internal Pull down resistor </text>
<text x="381" y="203.2" size="1.778" layer="91">this is 3.3V from voltage regulator</text>
<text x="452.12" y="-35.56" size="1.778" layer="91">make L2-PE0 internal pull down resistor</text>
<text x="406.4" y="33.02" size="1.778" layer="91">Base is same thing as sleeve</text>
<text x="342.9" y="-81.28" size="1.778" layer="91">**NOTE: STILL NEED TO GET LED GPIO TOGGLES TO BE AT LEAST 4MA MODE IN CASE ULN TRANSISTOR ARRAY TAKES MORE CURRENT THAN EXPECTED***</text>
<text x="127" y="-109.22" size="1.778" layer="91">added text :)</text>
<text x="363.22" y="-167.64" size="1.778" layer="91">idk what to connect this to? </text>
<text x="525.78" y="-157.48" size="1.778" layer="91">idk what to connect this to? </text>
</plain>
